Written by Anna Lo Piccolo
Last update: November 2025

2D (y-z directions) experiment used to implement and test an update of the
submesoscale parameterization, that follows work conducted by Anna Lo Piccolo
and Baylor Fox-Kemper at Brown University in 2025.

The parameterization consists of an update to the overturning streamfunction 
formulated by Fox-Kemper, Ferrari, Hallberg, 2008, and a Redi component adapted 
for entrainment/subduction problems.

1. The streamfunction psi is defined in submeso_calc_psi.F, and the parameterization
modifies the vertical structure function mu.

2. Redi diffusivity is added to the submesoscale subroutine so that a unique submeso_calc.F
is created.

Issues:
The mixed-layer depth computed in calc_oce_mxlayer.F does not represent the depth at which
buoyancy fluxes are zero.
